{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 8... Nbd7. Black develops the light-squared bishop before closing the diagonal with ...e6. ...c6 gives the queen c7 as a possible retreat and restrains Nb5. White has more central space and can play Ne5, Nd5 or d5 when supported. A routine pawn move may lose a crucial queen tempo. } 8... Nbd7 9. Qe2 Bb4 10. a3 Bxc3 *

