{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 8... Bb4. Qe2 prepares long castling and increases central pressure. ...Bb4 develops with a concrete relation to the c3 knight rather than immediately making another pawn move. White can play O-O-O and advance the kingside pawns. Opening the center while your own king remains on e8 can be dangerous. } 8... Bb4 9. a3 Nbd7 10. O-O-O Bxc3 *

